# LINE ENDINGS
#
# `.prettierrc` sets endOfLine: "crlf", and 435 of the 458 source files already are —
# but nothing enforced it, so 23 files had quietly drifted to LF or to a mix of both.
# That was 2,035 lint errors: 70% of the entire frontend lint run, saying nothing
# whatever about the code, and drowning the ~840 findings that do.
#
# Without this file the answer depends on each machine's core.autocrlf, which means a
# fresh clone can reintroduce the whole problem. eol=crlf pins it for every checkout on
# every platform, so the working tree always matches what Prettier is configured to want.
* text=auto eol=crlf

# The exceptions, which must stay LF wherever they run.
# gradlew is a shell script — CRLF makes the shebang unusable and the Android build
# fails with "bad interpreter" on any Linux runner.
android/gradlew text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf

# Never touched, never diffed.
*.jar binary
*.keystore binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.pdf binary
